<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Persia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Persia is the historical name for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, derived from the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pars">Pars</a> in the south-west. It was the heartland of the Achaemenid, Parthian and Sasanian empires and later of the Safavid, Afsharid and Zand dynasties. Conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, it also exerted a profound cultural influence on its conquerors, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/persia.jpg" alt="Persia" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SVG file: SiBr4Designer: Hamid NadimiConstruction: ISIRI · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iran_(official).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
